---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About — Siddharth Sahoo"
  description="About Siddharth Sahoo: developer, visual creator and builder of software, automations and internet things."
  pageClass="about-page"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <span class="kicker">03 / About</span>
    <h1>One person. Two toolkits.</h1>
    <div class="page-hero-copy">
      <div class="micro">SID / FLAC / 11SID11</div>
      <p>I am Siddharth Sahoo. I build software, edit video, design visual work and usually end up turning recurring annoyances into small products.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="shell" style="padding-bottom:clamp(5rem,10vw,10rem)">
    <div class="about-grid">
      <article class="about-block" data-reveal>
        <span class="kicker">Developer</span>
        <h2>I like products with boundaries.</h2>
        <p>Local-first software, automation, browser tooling, PWAs and systems where the architecture explains what the product refuses to do as clearly as what it does.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="about-block" data-reveal>
        <span class="kicker">Creative</span>
        <h2>I edit around attention.</h2>
        <p>Gaming and YouTube work taught me to notice where energy dies. That same instinct carries into thumbnails, brand content and visual systems: <strong>make the point readable, then get out of its way.</strong></p>
      </article>
      <article class="about-block" data-reveal>
        <span class="kicker">Workflow</span>
        <h2>AI is infrastructure now.</h2>
        <p>Claude and Codex are heavily integrated into how I investigate, build and iterate. They increase range and speed; source control, tests, explicit constraints and human review keep the output accountable.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="about-block" data-reveal>
        <span class="kicker">Away from the screen</span>
        <h2>Games, cameras, music, food, places.</h2>
        <p>Photography is usually the excuse to notice light. Gaming is partly recreation and partly an endless study in interface, pacing and feedback. I also sing, play guitar badly enough to keep learning, cook, and travel when the calendar cooperates.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="contact-band" aria-label="Social profiles">
    <div data-reveal>
      <span class="kicker">Talk</span>
      <h2>Internet coordinates.</h2>
      <p>X and Discord are the most direct ways to reach me. GitHub is where the code is. Instagram is where the visual side leaks out.</p>
    </div>
    <div data-reveal>
      <span class="kicker">Elsewhere</span>
      <div class="contact-actions">
        <a class="cta-button" href="https://x.com/sid_flac" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">X / @sid_flac ↗</a>
        <a class="cta-button" href="https://discord.com/users/456027988417314816" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Discord ↗</a>
        <a class="cta-button" href="https://github.com/11sid11" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub / 11sid11 ↗</a>
        <a class="cta-button" href="https://www.instagram.com/sid.flac/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Instagram / @sid.flac ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
